      "math_academy_id": "e-66",
      "problem": "Find $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}g(x)$ for the function given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14259217/assets/c624be0e55dc5aa7f931d062ead2cfa05360e9f6bb449a8a62535f3a71b02131.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "To compute $\\lim\\limits_{x \\to \\, 1} g(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the right-sided limit $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1^+}g(x)$ does not exist since $g(x)$ is not defined in the interval $x\\in(1,2).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow 1}g(x) = \\text{DNE}.\n$$",
